---
description: Dr Non's anti-slop design rules. Read ANTI-SLOP.md before any UI work.
alwaysApply: true
---

Before designing or changing any page, component, style or chart, read `ANTI-SLOP.md` at the repo root and follow its hard limits: empty space is a decision, subtract before you add, the map comes first. Run `node tools/slop-lint.mjs <url>` before calling UI work done.

Also enforce the glance-path and kinetic-grid rules in `ANTI-SLOP.md` (section "Glance path and kinetic grid"). Canonical text: Nonarkara/Non-Slop `MSH.md`, read with `ANTI-SLOP.md`. `STYLE.md` wins.

- Visual gravity: headline and primary action on the exit of the dominant visual. Critical text does not sit in a dead zone above a heavy hero.
- No leapfrog: related copy does not jump a massive image.
- Kinetic grid: extreme scale contrast; break a layout rule on the grid; negative space stays active; one or two accents, and no third shout.
- Motion: snap, or show the skeleton first. Do not float or morph.
